# Mercury Edit 2 — findings by Inkling 2 Small

- Source: Inception Labs (`inception/mercury-edit-2`)
- Date: 2026-11-13 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** Mercury Edit 2
- **Short description:** Inception Labs' diffusion LLM purpose-built for next-edit prediction and code autocomplete — FIM (`v1/fim/completions`) and NextEdit (`v1/edit/completions`) endpoints; parallel denoising for low-latency Tab completions; KTO-aligned with human edit-preference data. Available on the Inception Platform and integrated in Zed. Text-only, specialized — not a general chat model.
- **Provider / access:** Inception API — `https://api.inceptionlabs.ai/v1` — endpoints `v1/fim/completions` and `v1/edit/completions`; also callable from Zed's edit-prediction providers; launched 2026-10-29 (blog; GA on the platform).
- **Release / knowledge:** 2026-10-29 (Introducing Mercury Edit 2). Knowledge cutoff not published.
- **IDs:** `mercury-edit-2` (Inception Platform). Listed on OpenRouter as `inception/mercury-edit-2` per third-party trackers (specs only, no eval rows).
- **Context window:** FIM 32K / NextEdit 32K total; max output 8,192 (Inception docs, verified 2026-11-13; third-party trackers list 128K/8K — official docs win).
- **Modalities:** text in; text out. No tool calling, no structured outputs, no image input — specialized completion endpoints only.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-13):** $0.25 in / $0.75 out per 1M; cached input $0.025. New accounts get 10M free tokens; Zed users get one free month of Mercury Edit 2 suggestions.
- **Architecture:** proprietary diffusion LLM (dLLM); parameter count not published.

### Raw benchmarks found

Inception's launch blog reports relative results only — **no absolute scores are published for this exact ID**:

- Edits accepted **48% more often** than its predecessor; **27% more selective** in edits shown (KTO-aligned; internal measurement)
- Quality claim: "superior quality and speed to alternatives" on a four-benchmark internal suite — Instinct (continuedev), FIM (openai/human-eval-infilling, validated by running test cases), Next-edit Prediction (NEP, lurf21), plus one internal next-edit benchmark; final quality = average of the four; alternatives included custom next-edit models and speed-optimized frontier models. **No numbers disclosed.**
- Speed: end-to-end latency measured on "a set of representative requests"; Mercury Edit 2 faster than alternatives — **no absolute latency published**
- SWE-bench / Terminal-Bench / LiveCodeBench / HumanEval-infilling absolute% / AA-Index: no verified public score found
- SerenitiesAI and BenchLM list the model (pricing/specs only; zero task-score rows; "specifications last checked 2026-09-14")

Agent / tool use:

- no verified public score found (no tools/structured outputs supported — specialized FIM/NextEdit endpoints)

Reasoning / knowledge:

- no verified public score found

Coding:

- no verified public absolute score found (official positioning: next-edit/autocomplete; vendor-internal relative gains only: +48% accept rate, +27% selectivity)

Long context:

- 32K FIM/NextEdit window per official docs; no verified public long-context retrieval score found

